course: dictionary
lesson: 9586
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around the word. Those words are its context, and they leave clues. «The room was full of party streamers.» Here, streamers are long, narrow strips of coloured paper or ribbon used to decorate for a party.
explain: The same word can mean something new in a different sentence. «Her favourite streamer plays video games live every evening.» Here, a streamer is a person who broadcasts live video online, and the people watching are the audience.
explain: A third meaning is a long flag or ribbon that flows out in the wind. «A kite had a long red streamer flapping in the wind.» The kite and the wind are the clues. Check your choice by putting the meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Streamers» can mean paper or ribbon for party decorations, or people who broadcast live online.
fact: Some streamers earn a lot, but most earn little or nothing, and streaming is hard work.
fact: Never share personal details, such as your address or school, in a streamer's chat.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The room was full of party streamers.» What does streamers mean here? | People who play games live online | *Long strips of coloured paper or ribbon for decorating | Flags that blow in the wind | Lights that flash at night
exercise: «Her favourite streamer plays video games live every evening.» What is a streamer in this sentence? | *A person who broadcasts live video online | A type of kite | A long ribbon on a bike | Paper hung from the ceiling
exercise: «A kite had a long red streamer flapping in the wind.» What does streamer mean here? | A sweet, sticky drink | *A long, narrow strip that streams out in the wind | A person who plays games live | A party decoration on a wall
test: «Some streamers earn a lot, but most earn little or nothing.» What does this tell you about streaming? | Streamers never make videos | *Only a few streamers earn a lot, and streaming is hard work | Streaming is always free to watch | Everyone who streams becomes rich
test: Which meaning fits «a streamer's chat»? | *Messages from people talking with a live streamer online | A ribbon hanging in a chat room | A strong gust of wind | Paper chains at a party
exam: Which is the best advice about a streamer's chat? | Post a photo of yourself for everyone to see | *Never share personal details, such as your home address or school | Tell them your password | Share your home address so they can write back
